  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce morbidity and mortality caused by malaria in the various epidemiological zones by two thirds of the 2015 level by 2020 - Kenya (01-Jan-2018-30-Jun-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya, Malaria, Amref Health Africa (Amref Kenya)This program has the following goals: To reduce morbidity and mortality caused by malaria in the various epidemiological zones by two thirds of the 2015 level by 2020. The objectives of this program are: To have at least80% of people living in malaria risk areas using appropriate malaria preventive interventions by 2020.  To have 100% of all suspected malaria cases presenting to a health provider managed according to the national malaria treatment guidelines by 2020.  To have at least80% of people living in malaria risk areas using appropriate malaria preventive interventions by 2020.  To increase utilization of all malaria control interventions by target communities in Kenya to at least 80% by 2020 and sustain thereafter.  Ensure that all levels (national, counties, sub-counties) provide reports on at least 80% of core malaria indicators according to the national M &amp; E plan by 2020.  To increase capacity in coordination, leadership, governance and resource mobilization at all levels towards achievement of the malaria program objectives by 2020</narrative>
  </description>
